 as long to do it but  Americans average 13,000 476 miles each  year if you did want to beat Columbus's  voyage in one trip you do have a couple  options first this monstrosity this  crazy road trip was designed to be the  most efficient way to visit 50 national  landmarks within the 48 contiguous  United States at a whopping thirteen  thousand six hundred ninety nine miles  its creator estimates it would take  without traffic 224 hours of driving or  9.3 full 24 hour days to finish it a  realistic estimate would be more along  the lines of two to three months to  actually do it and enjoy the experience  if you decided to tackle the landmark  road trip you could officially say you  traveled a greater distance faster than  the man credited with discovering North  America if you wanted to add another  trophy to your collection you could  drive another 4,000 miles or so to outdo  Ferdinand Magellan or rather the small  number of his crew that survived the  first expedition to circumnavigate the  globe Magellan set sail from Spain in  1519 with a fleet of five ships hoping  to discover a western sea route to the  Spice Islands of the 270 crew members  that set out at the end of the three  year journey only eighteen men remained  Magellan himself was killed by a poison  arrow during a battle with Island  natives all in all the length of the  expedition totalled an impressive 18,000  95 miles to beat that distance you'd  have to complete the enormous landmark  road trip and then drive across the  entire United States coast-to-coast  twice the shortest distance from one  coast of the US to the other is about  2,000 miles if you do decide to dethrone  Magellan just make sure you don't pick a  fight with any locals lest you repeat  history even more well-traveled than  those on the Magellan expedition was  Venetian merchant marco polo polo spent  24 years of his life cataloguing his  adventures in china including his  experiences with Kublai Khan son of the  legendary jingis Khan these epic tales  would later inspire another Explorer on  our list Christopher Columbus over his  24 years of travel and adventure Marco  Polo had accumulated an amazing 20 3339  miles  mostly over land to beat polos distance  you'd have to start with the landmark  road trip and then tackle the crazy  Mongol Rally heralded as the greatest  adventure in the world the Mongol Rally  is a 10,000 mile Odyssey across the  mountains desert and steppe throughout  Europe and Asia terminating in the  Russian city of Gulen du-de of course a  10,000 mile journey across 22 countries  would be too easy without a few more  restrictions to take part in the annual  rally you have to raise $1,000 for  charity and find a cheap sub  ten-year-old car with a 1.2 liter engine  or smaller if you can tackle the Mongol  Rally and the u.s. landmark road trip in  under 24 years  congratulations you've traveled farther  and faster than the legendary Marco Polo  finally there's one adventurer on our  list that you'd really really have to  try to top and you've probably never  heard of  born in 1906 canadian-american Idris  Welsh would go on to adopt the name  aloha wander well and drive over 500,000  miles in early Ford automobiles as a  teenager wander well joined an  expedition to travel the world by Ford  Model T Model A and the later touring  sedan she and her first husband cap  wander well recorded their adventures on  sixteen and thirty five millimeter film  in locations across 80 countries and 6  continents always in their trusty Fords  Aloha was the first woman to  circumnavigate the world by car and all  of her films now reside in the Hollywood  Academy Film Archives so still want to  take her title of 500,000 miles here's  how you do it step one complete the US  landmark road trip step two defeat the  mighty Mongol Rally step three  survive the 30 thousand mile behemoth  that is the pan-american highway  starting way up in Deadhorse Alaska and  ending up all the way down into swaiiow  Argentina those three trips will rack up  an impressive 53 thousand six hundred  ninety nine miles just over a hundred  miles fewer than Columbus Magellan and  polo combined but that still nowhere  near Aloha wander wells mileage you'd  have to complete those three giant road  trips ten times to claim the trophy of  being more adventurous than the world's  most widely traveled woman could you do  it with enough time and dedication sure  just don't expect me to go with you even  if I do drive a Ford if you wanted to  learn about the issues you would face on  a road trip with friends or your spouse  it doesn't matter that five percent of  road trips result in irreparable harm to  the relationship or any number of other  facts what matters is the actual road  trip that you take and how you react to  it I'm sure most of us agree that the  best way to learn anything is by  actually doing it yourself for all the  students and young professionals in my  audience and I know there are a lot of  you whether you're struggling to make  sense of math or want to challenge your  understanding of physics brilliant org  has the best way for you to learn by  actually solving interesting puzzles  what better way to build up your  understanding of a concept than learning  how to think like a scientist put  yourself in Christopher Columbus's shoes  if you didn't trust the contemporary  estimates of the Earth's diameter  brilliant could help guide you in  understanding how to make these  calculations so you wouldn't have  drastically underestimated the length of  the  and ended up with a mutinous crew the  great part is even when you get a  question wrong  brilliant tells you exactly why your  answer was incorrect and shows you the  steps to finding the right solution as a  little thank you for watching my videos  the first 200 people to sign up at  brilliant org slash second thought will  get 20% off their premium subscription  so if you want to avoid a mutiny on your  next road 